outputs.L1:
The invention relates to a fluoroelastomer composition comprising:

(a) a vinylidene fluoride-based fluoroelastomer [fluoroelastomer (A)] comprising recurring units derived from vinylidene fluoride (VDF) and recurring units derived from at least one additional (per)fluorinated monomer, wherein said fluoroelastomer (A):

- has a polydispersity index (IMWD) ranging from 1.5 to 3.5;
- comprises polar end groups of formula —CF2CH2OH in an amount of at least 3 mmol/kg and at most 6 mmol/kg; and
- further comprises end-of-chain groups of formula —CF2H, —CF2CH3, and, optionally, —OC(0)—RH, wherein RH is a C1–C6 alkyl group, in an amount satisfying the following inequality:

  [—CF2CH2OH] + [—CF2H] + [—CF2CH3H—OC(0)RH] ≤ 30 + (2 × 10^6)/Mn;

(b) at least one polyhydroxylated curing agent;

(c) at least one accelerant;

(d) at least one metal oxide selected from the group consisting of divalent metal oxides; and

(e) optionally, at least one metal hydroxide, wherein, if present, the amount of said metal hydroxide is less than 3 phr, based on 100 parts by weight of fluoroelastomer (A).

outputs.L2:
The invention relates to a fluoroelastomer formulation containing the following components:

(a) a vinylidene fluoride (VDF)-based fluoroelastomer, designated fluoroelastomer (A), having repeating units originating from VDF and repeating units originating from at least one other (per)fluorinated monomer. Fluoroelastomer (A):

- has a polydispersity index (IMWD) ranging from 1.5 to 3.5;
- contains from 3 mmol/kg to 6 mmol/kg of polar terminal groups represented by —CF2CH2OH; and
- also contains chain-end groups represented by —CF2H and —CF2CH3 and, optionally, —OC(0)—RH, where RH denotes a C1–C6 alkyl group, in quantities that meet the following condition:

[—CF2CH2OH] + [—CF2H] + [—CF2CH3H—OC(0)RH] ≤ 30 + (2 × 10^6)/Mn;

(b) at least one polyhydroxylated curing agent;

(c) one or more accelerants;

(d) at least one divalent metal oxide; and

(e) optionally, at least one metal hydroxide, provided that, when present, the metal hydroxide is used in an amount of less than 3 phr per 100 parts by weight of fluoroelastomer (A).

